# The ledger of `amqp`: what a program does with an AMQP 0-9-1 server,
# measured against Go's github.com/rabbitmq/amqp091-go v1.17.0 (its `go doc
# -all`, fetched into the scratch folder on 2026-11-18), Python's pika 1.5.0
# (`dir` of `pika`, `BlockingConnection`, `BlockingChannel`,
# `ConnectionParameters`, `BasicProperties`, `pika.exceptions`, installed into
# the scratch folder the same day) and Rust's lapin 4.12.3 (its docs.rs pages
# read the same day: the crate's items, `Channel` and `Connection`).
#
# The expected values of the tests were asked of pika: the bytes of every
# method the client sends (`pika.frame.Method(...).marshal()`), of a content
# header with every property (`pika.frame.Header`), of a field table with
# every type (`pika.data.encode_table`) and what it reads for each letter
# (`pika.data.decode_table`); and of amqp091-go and pika both, how a URL is
# read (`amqp.ParseURI`, `pika.URLParameters`). The live run, on 2026-11-18,
# reached RabbitMQ 4.0.5 of Debian 13 in a container of this Mac: PLAIN and
# AMQPLAIN, a virtual host, permissions refused, TLS.

capability amqp/connect  a connection made: the protocol's header, the login, the settings agreed, the virtual host opened
  heroes  amqp.connect, amqp.options, amqp.Options, amqp.Connection, amqp.DEFAULT_PORT, amqp.DEFAULT_TLS_PORT
  go      Dial, DialConfig, Config, Config.Vhost, Open, Connection
  rust    Connection::connect, Connection::connect_with_config, Connection::connect_uri, Connection::connect_uri_with_config, Connection::connect_with_runtime, Connection::connect_uri_with_runtime, ConnectionProperties, Configuration, Connection::configuration, ConnectionBuilder, DefaultConnectionBuilder
  python  BlockingConnection, ConnectionParameters, ConnectionParameters.host, ConnectionParameters.port, ConnectionParameters.virtual_host, ConnectionParameters.socket_timeout, ConnectionParameters.stack_timeout, AMQPConnectionWorkflow
  note    one blocking client, as pika's BlockingConnection; the callback adapters (SelectConnection and the others) are the `poll` capability's

capability amqp/url  the options a URL names, as RabbitMQ writes one
  heroes  amqp.parse_url
  go      ParseURI, URI, URI.String, URI.PlainAuth, URI.AMQPlainAuth
  rust    Connection::connect_uri
  python  URLParameters
  note    an empty path and `/` are the virtual host `/` (Go and pika agree); a path of two segments is refused, where Go joins them and pika keeps the first; a frame of 4096 bytes is taken, AMQP's own minimum, where pika asks 8192

capability amqp/tls  TLS from the first byte, the server's certificate checked against the system's store or the roots given
  heroes  amqp.Options (tls, roots)
  go      DialTLS, Config.TLSClientConfig, Connection.ConnectionState
  rust    Connection::connector, Connect
  python  SSLOptions, ConnectionParameters.ssl_options
  note    a client certificate is not presented, which `tls` does not offer; ConnectionState's details are `tls.version_of` and `tls.protocol_of`'s, which take the stream `stream_of` answers

capability amqp/login  a user's name and a password, by PLAIN or RabbitMQ's AMQPLAIN
  heroes  amqp.Options (username, password, mechanism), amqp.Mechanism
  go      PlainAuth, AMQPlainAuth, Config.SASL, Authentication
  rust    auth::AuthProvider, auth::DefaultTokenProvider
  python  PlainCredentials, ConnectionParameters.credentials
  note    a login refused is `permission`: RabbitMQ closes the connection with 403 where the client says it reads authentication_failure_close, which this one does

capability amqp/login-external  a login by the TLS client's certificate (EXTERNAL)
  heroes  refused: `tls` presents no client certificate, so there is nothing for EXTERNAL to name
  go      DialTLS_ExternalAuth, ExternalAuth
  rust    -
  python  pika.credentials.ExternalCredentials

capability amqp/login-token  a login by a token that expires, renewed on an open connection
  heroes  amqp.update_secret
  go      Connection.UpdateSecret
  rust    Connection::update_secret, auth::TokenProvider, auth::TokenAuthProvider
  python  BlockingConnection.update_secret

capability amqp/tune  the heartbeat, the largest frame and the channels agreed, and what the server said of itself
  heroes  amqp.Options (heartbeat, frame_max, channel_max), amqp.server_of, amqp.Server
  go      Config.Heartbeat, Config.FrameSize, Config.ChannelMax, FrameSizeUnlimited, Connection.Properties, Connection.Major, Connection.Minor, Connection.Locales, Connection.Config
  rust    Configuration
  python  ConnectionParameters.heartbeat, ConnectionParameters.frame_max, ConnectionParameters.channel_max, BlockingConnection.publisher_confirms_supported, BlockingConnection.basic_nack_supported, BlockingConnection.consumer_cancel_notify_supported, BlockingConnection.exchange_exchange_bindings_supported, BlockingConnection.publisher_confirms, BlockingConnection.basic_nack, BlockingConnection.consumer_cancel_notify, BlockingConnection.exchange_exchange_bindings
  note    each setting is the smaller of the two where neither side says 0, the other's where one does, as amqp091-go agrees them; the capabilities pika asks one by one are `server_of`'s properties, `capabilities` among them

capability amqp/client-properties  the client's properties, its name and its locale told to the server
  heroes  amqp.Options (connection_name, properties, locale)
  go      Config.Properties, Config.Locale, NewConnectionProperties, Table.SetClientConnectionName
  rust    ConnectionProperties
  python  ConnectionParameters.client_properties, ConnectionParameters.locale

capability amqp/close  a connection closed, by the program or the server, and why
  heroes  amqp.close, amqp.is_closed, amqp.closing_of, amqp.Closing
  go      Connection.Close, Connection.CloseDeadline, Connection.IsClosed, Connection.NotifyClose, Error, Error.Code, Error.Reason, Error.Server
  rust    Connection::close, Connection::status, ConnectionStatus, ConnectionState, Error, ErrorKind
  python  BlockingConnection.close, BlockingConnection.is_closed, BlockingConnection.is_open, ConnectionClosed, ConnectionClosedByBroker, ConnectionClosedByClient, AMQPConnectionError
  note    `close` waits `Options.wait` for the answer, as CloseDeadline's deadline

capability amqp/blocked  whether the server holds the connection's publishes back, as RabbitMQ does when its memory or disk runs short
  heroes  amqp.blocked_of, amqp.Blocked
  go      Connection.NotifyBlocked, Blocking
  rust    -
  python  BlockingConnection.add_on_connection_blocked_callback, BlockingConnection.add_on_connection_unblocked_callback, ConnectionParameters.blocked_connection_timeout, ConnectionBlockedTimeout

capability amqp/heartbeat  the heartbeat sent and read while the program waits, and the connection kept with nothing else to do
  heroes  amqp.idle
  go      -
  rust    Connection::run
  python  BlockingConnection.process_data_events, BlockingConnection.sleep, AMQPHeartbeatTimeout
  note    the heartbeat is sent while a call waits, the program's own loop being the only one, as pika's blocking connection does

capability amqp/poll  many connections waited on by one thread, each read when its stream is readable
  heroes  amqp.stream_of, amqp.read_ready, amqp.held_of
  go      -
  rust    runtime::default_runtime
  python  SelectConnection, BlockingConnection.call_later, BlockingConnection.remove_timeout, BlockingConnection.add_callback_threadsafe
  note    `poll` waits; this package reads what the stream holds and keeps what it brings

capability amqp/addresses  the connection's own address and the server's
  heroes  pending: `net.Conn` holds both, and the session keeps only the stream; a field of the connection's addresses waits for a face change
  go      Connection.LocalAddr, Connection.RemoteAddr
  rust    -
  python  -

capability amqp/channels  a channel opened, closed, and why the server closed it
  heroes  amqp.open_channel, amqp.close_channel, amqp.is_channel_open, amqp.channel_closing_of, amqp.Channel
  go      Connection.Channel, Channel.Close, Channel.IsClosed, Channel.NotifyClose
  rust    Connection::create_channel, Channel::close, Channel::id, Channel::status, ChannelStatus, ChannelState
  python  BlockingConnection.channel, BlockingChannel.close, BlockingChannel.is_closed, BlockingChannel.is_open, BlockingChannel.channel_number, ChannelClosed, ChannelClosedByBroker, ChannelClosedByClient, ChannelWrongStateError, NoFreeChannels
  note    a channel the server closes (a queue not found, a declaration that disagrees) stays closed and says why; the program opens another

capability amqp/qos  the prefetch: how much the server sends before the consumer acknowledges
  heroes  amqp.qos
  go      Channel.Qos
  rust    Channel::basic_qos, options::BasicQosOptions, ChannelQos
  python  BlockingChannel.basic_qos

capability amqp/flow  the server asked to stop or go on sending to a channel, and its own asking told
  heroes  amqp.flow
  go      Channel.Flow, Channel.NotifyFlow
  rust    Channel::channel_flow, options::ChannelFlowOptions, options::ChannelFlowOkOptions
  python  BlockingChannel.flow
  note    RabbitMQ refuses active false with 540 (`unsupported`); a channel.flow from the server is answered and kept

capability amqp/exchanges  an exchange declared, of each kind, or only asked about
  heroes  amqp.declare_exchange, amqp.exchange, amqp.Exchange, amqp.DIRECT, amqp.FANOUT, amqp.TOPIC, amqp.HEADERS
  go      Channel.ExchangeDeclare, Channel.ExchangeDeclarePassive, ExchangeDirect, ExchangeFanout, ExchangeTopic, ExchangeHeaders, DefaultExchange
  rust    Channel::exchange_declare, options::ExchangeDeclareOptions, ExchangeKind
  python  BlockingChannel.exchange_declare, pika.exchange_type.ExchangeType

capability amqp/exchange-delete  an exchange deleted
  heroes  amqp.delete_exchange
  go      Channel.ExchangeDelete
  rust    Channel::exchange_delete, options::ExchangeDeleteOptions
  python  BlockingChannel.exchange_delete

capability amqp/exchange-bindings  an exchange bound to another and unbound (RabbitMQ's extension)
  heroes  amqp.bind_exchange, amqp.unbind_exchange
  go      Channel.ExchangeBind, Channel.ExchangeUnbind
  rust    Channel::exchange_bind, Channel::exchange_unbind, options::ExchangeBindOptions, options::ExchangeUnbindOptions
  python  BlockingChannel.exchange_bind, BlockingChannel.exchange_unbind

capability amqp/queues  a queue declared, named by the server or the program, or only asked about, with its arguments
  heroes  amqp.declare_queue, amqp.queue, amqp.Queue, amqp.Declared
  go      Channel.QueueDeclare, Channel.QueueDeclarePassive, Channel.QueueInspect, Queue, QueueTypeArg, QueueMaxLenArg, QueueMaxLenBytesArg, StreamMaxLenBytesArg, QueueOverflowArg, QueueMessageTTLArg, QueueTTLArg, StreamMaxAgeArg, StreamMaxSegmentSizeBytesArg, QueueVersionArg, ConsumerTimeoutArg, SingleActiveConsumerArg, QueueTypeClassic, QueueTypeQuorum, QueueTypeStream, QueueOverflowDropHead, QueueOverflowRejectPublish, QueueOverflowRejectPublishDLX
  rust    Channel::queue_declare, options::QueueDeclareOptions, Queue
  python  BlockingChannel.queue_declare
  note    the arguments are a field table the program writes, `x-queue-type` and the others by their names; Go's constants for them are text the program writes

capability amqp/queue-bindings  a queue bound to an exchange and unbound
  heroes  amqp.bind_queue, amqp.unbind_queue
  go      Channel.QueueBind, Channel.QueueUnbind
  rust    Channel::queue_bind, Channel::queue_unbind, options::QueueBindOptions
  python  BlockingChannel.queue_bind, BlockingChannel.queue_unbind

capability amqp/queue-purge  a queue emptied, its messages counted
  heroes  amqp.purge_queue
  go      Channel.QueuePurge
  rust    Channel::queue_purge, options::QueuePurgeOptions
  python  BlockingChannel.queue_purge

capability amqp/queue-delete  a queue deleted, if unused or empty where asked
  heroes  amqp.delete_queue
  go      Channel.QueueDelete
  rust    Channel::queue_delete, options::QueueDeleteOptions
  python  BlockingChannel.queue_delete

capability amqp/publish  a message published with its properties, its body cut into frames
  heroes  amqp.publish, amqp.message, amqp.Message, amqp.TRANSIENT, amqp.PERSISTENT
  go      Channel.Publish, Channel.PublishWithContext, Publishing, Transient, Persistent, NeverExpire, ImmediatelyExpire, MimeTextPlain, MimeApplicationJSON, MimeApplicationOctetStream, MimeApplicationXML, MimeTextXML, MimeApplicationProtobuf, MimeApplicationXProtobuf, MimeApplicationMsgPack, MimeApplicationAvro, MimeApplicationCloudEventsJSON, MimeApplicationFormURLEncoded
  rust    Channel::basic_publish, options::BasicPublishOptions, BasicProperties, AMQPProperties
  python  BlockingChannel.basic_publish, BasicProperties, DeliveryMode, BodyTooLongError, MessageBodyTooLargeError
  note    a property AMQP leaves out is the empty text, the empty list or 0, as amqp091-go reads it; a timestamp of 0 is left out, where pika writes it; the MIME types and expirations are text the program writes

capability amqp/mandatory  a mandatory message no queue takes, handed back and read
  heroes  amqp.next_return, amqp.Return, amqp.REPLY_NO_ROUTE
  go      Channel.NotifyReturn, Return
  rust    message::BasicReturnMessage
  python  BlockingChannel.add_on_return_callback, UnroutableError

capability amqp/immediate  a message dropped where no consumer takes it at once (the immediate flag)
  heroes  refused: RabbitMQ refuses it since 3.0, closing the connection; a message's time to live of 0 does what it did
  go      Channel.Publish (immediate)
  rust    options::BasicPublishOptions (immediate)
  python  -

capability amqp/confirms  publisher confirms: a channel in confirm mode, each publish numbered, confirmed or refused, waited for one or all
  heroes  amqp.select_confirms, amqp.next_confirmation, amqp.wait_confirms, amqp.Confirmation, amqp.publish
  go      Channel.Confirm, Channel.NotifyConfirm, Channel.NotifyPublish, Confirmation, Channel.PublishWithDeferredConfirm, Channel.PublishWithDeferredConfirmWithContext, DeferredConfirmation, DeferredConfirmation.Acked, DeferredConfirmation.Done, DeferredConfirmation.Wait, DeferredConfirmation.WaitContext, Channel.GetNextPublishSeqNo
  rust    Channel::confirm_select, options::ConfirmSelectOptions, PublisherConfirm, Confirmation, Channel::wait_for_confirms
  python  BlockingChannel.confirm_delivery, NackError
  note    `publish` answers the sequence number, Go's GetNextPublishSeqNo; a confirmation of several at once is answered one publish at a time

capability amqp/consume  a consumer started and its deliveries read, from every channel in the order they came
  heroes  amqp.consume, amqp.consumer, amqp.Consumer, amqp.next_delivery, amqp.Delivery
  go      Channel.Consume, Channel.ConsumeWithContext, Delivery
  rust    Channel::basic_consume, options::BasicConsumeOptions, options::BasicDeliverOptions, Consumer, message::Delivery, message::DeliveryResult, ConsumerDelegate
  python  BlockingChannel.basic_consume, BlockingChannel.consume, BlockingChannel.start_consuming, BlockingChannel.stop_consuming, BlockingChannel.get_waiting_message_count, BlockingChannel.consumer_tags, DuplicateConsumerTag
  note    the deliveries held are bounded by `Options.most_held`, past which the connection closes failing `limit`; `qos` keeps the server from sending more

capability amqp/cancel  a consumer ended by the program, or by the server where its queue goes
  heroes  amqp.cancel, amqp.cancellations_of, amqp.Cancellation
  go      Channel.Cancel, Channel.NotifyCancel
  rust    Channel::basic_cancel, options::BasicCancelOptions
  python  BlockingChannel.basic_cancel, BlockingChannel.cancel, BlockingChannel.add_on_cancel_callback, ConsumerCancelled

capability amqp/get  one message taken from a queue
  heroes  amqp.get
  go      Channel.Get
  rust    Channel::basic_get, options::BasicGetOptions, options::BasicGetOkOptions, message::BasicGetMessage
  python  BlockingChannel.basic_get
  note    an empty queue is `not_found`, where Go answers ok false and pika (None, None, None)

capability amqp/acknowledge  a delivery acknowledged, refused, or requeued, one or every one up to it
  heroes  amqp.ack, amqp.nack, amqp.reject
  go      Channel.Ack, Channel.Nack, Channel.Reject, Delivery.Ack, Delivery.Nack, Delivery.Reject, Acknowledger
