capability amqp/transactions  a channel made transactional, committed, rolled back
  heroes  amqp.select_transactions, amqp.commit, amqp.rollback
  go      Channel.Tx, Channel.TxCommit, Channel.TxRollback
  rust    Channel::tx_select, Channel::tx_commit, Channel::tx_rollback
  python  BlockingChannel.tx_select, BlockingChannel.tx_commit, BlockingChannel.tx_rollback

capability amqp/field-tables  field tables read and written, every type RabbitMQ knows, a field found by its name
  heroes  amqp.encode_table, amqp.decode_table, amqp.value_of, amqp.Field, amqp.Value
  go      Table, Table.Validate, Decimal
  rust    amq_protocol_types::FieldTable, amq_protocol_types::AMQPValue
  python  pika.data.encode_table, pika.data.decode_table, pika.data.encode_value, pika.data.decode_value, InvalidFieldTypeException, UnsupportedAMQPFieldException, UnencodableDecimalError, UnencodableFloatError, UnencodableLongError, UnencodableTimestampError
  note    RabbitMQ's letters, as pika and Go write them (`s` a 16-bit integer, `l` a 64-bit one, `x` bytes); the standard's own `U` and `L` are read too; a long string that is not UTF-8 is read as bytes, as pika does; nesting is 64 deep at most, read without the stack

capability amqp/reply-codes  the reply codes of the protocol, and the code of Rebel's each one fails with
  heroes  amqp.REPLY_SUCCESS, amqp.REPLY_CONTENT_TOO_LARGE, amqp.REPLY_NO_ROUTE, amqp.REPLY_NO_CONSUMERS, amqp.REPLY_CONNECTION_FORCED, amqp.REPLY_INVALID_PATH, amqp.REPLY_ACCESS_REFUSED, amqp.REPLY_NOT_FOUND, amqp.REPLY_RESOURCE_LOCKED, amqp.REPLY_PRECONDITION_FAILED, amqp.REPLY_FRAME_ERROR, amqp.REPLY_SYNTAX_ERROR, amqp.REPLY_COMMAND_INVALID, amqp.REPLY_CHANNEL_ERROR, amqp.REPLY_UNEXPECTED_FRAME, amqp.REPLY_RESOURCE_ERROR, amqp.REPLY_NOT_ALLOWED, amqp.REPLY_NOT_IMPLEMENTED, amqp.REPLY_INTERNAL_ERROR
  go      ContentTooLarge, NoRoute, NoConsumers, ConnectionForced, InvalidPath, AccessRefused, NotFound, ResourceLocked, PreconditionFailed, FrameError, SyntaxError, CommandInvalid, ChannelError, UnexpectedFrame, ResourceError, NotAllowed, NotImplemented, InternalError, Error.Recover, Error.Recoverable, Error.Temporary
  rust    AMQPError, AMQPErrorKind, AMQPHardError, AMQPSoftError
  python  AMQPError, AMQPChannelError, ChannelError, ProbableAccessDeniedError, ProbableAuthenticationError, AuthenticationError, IncompatibleProtocolError, ProtocolVersionMismatch, ProtocolSyntaxError, InvalidChannelNumber, InvalidFrameError, FrameTooLargeError, UnexpectedFrameError, MethodNotImplemented, StreamLostError, ConnectionOpenAborted, ConnectionWrongStateError, ReentrancyError
  note    403 and 530 are `permission`; 404, 312 and 313 `not_found`; 311 `limit`; 320 `closed`; 540 `unsupported`; 402, 406 and 501 to 506 `invalid`; the rest `failed`; the message carries the code and the server's text

capability amqp/methods  the protocol's methods written and read one by one, as values
  heroes  refused: the frames are this client's to write and read, each function above sends the method it names; a second surface of the same methods would let a program write a frame that leaves the connection's state unknown to the client
  go      -
  rust    every gen_* and parse_* of the classes access, basic, channel, confirm, connection, exchange, queue and tx, AMQPClass, each class's AMQPMethod and the records of its methods
  python  pika.spec, pika.frame, pika.amqp_object

capability amqp/access-request  the access.request of AMQP 0-8
  heroes  refused: AMQP 0-9-1 deprecates it and RabbitMQ ignores it
  go      -
  rust    Channel::access_request, options::AccessRequestOptions
  python  -

capability amqp/no-wait  a declaration, binding or consumer sent without awaiting its answer
  heroes  refused: the server's refusal then closes the channel under a later call, which cannot say which request it was; every request here waits for its answer
  go      the noWait parameters of ExchangeDeclare, QueueDeclare, QueueBind, Consume and the others
  rust    the nowait fields of the options records
  python  -

capability amqp/recovery  a lost connection made again by the client, its channels, consumers and declarations redone
  heroes  refused: a connection lost takes its unacknowledged deliveries and unconfirmed publishes with it, so redoing the rest in silence would deliver some messages twice and lose the count of others; the program connects and declares anew, which it can see
  go      Recovery, ReconnectionConfig, ReconnectionConfig.Clone, ConnectionRecovery, DefaultConnectionRecovery, TopologyRecovery, DefaultTopologyRecovery, TopologyConfiguration, TopologyConfiguration.Clone, TopologyRecoveryEntity, TopologyRecoveryEntityType, TopologyRecoveryMode, Channel.TopologyConfiguration, Connection.Reconnect, Channel.Reconnect, Connection.IsRecoveryEnabled, Connection.IsConnectionRecoveryEnabled, Connection.IsTopologyRecoveryEnabled, Connection.MaxRetryCount, Connection.RetryInterval, Connection.NotifyRecoveryCancel, Channel.NotifyRecoveryCancel, Connection.NotifyStateChange, Channel.NotifyStateChange, StateChanged, LifeCycleState, DefaultMaxRetryCount, DefaultRetryInterval, BindingConfig, ExchangeConfig, ExchangeBindingConfig, QueueConfig, QosConfig
  rust    Channel::wait_for_recovery
  python  ConnectionParameters.connection_attempts, ConnectionParameters.retry_delay

dropped
  go      SetLogger, Logging, NullLogger (logging; a failure here is a value), DefaultDial, Config.Dial (a dialer the program writes, which needs a closure), Authentication's methods Mechanism and Response (an interface), Error.Error, Error.GoString (Go's error interface), Config.Recovery (the recovery refused above)
  rust    Connection::events_listener, Event (a listener of the connection's events, which needs a closure), runtime::default_runtime's executors, Connect (a trait for the program's own socket), auth::TokenProvider's implementations beyond the token itself, Result, Error's conversions
  python  every callback of SelectConnection and the adapters (on_open, on_close and the others), pika.logging, pika.diagnostic_utils, pika.tcp_socket_opts, ConnectionParameters.tcp_options, ConnectionParameters.max_inbound_message_body_size (here `Options.most_body_bytes`), ConnectionParameters.MAX_INBOUND_MESSAGE_BODY_SIZE_LIMIT, pika.validators, pika.callback, pika.heartbeat (the heartbeat checker, here the waiting call's), WorkQueueFullError, DuplicateGetOkCallback (callback plumbing)
